# fat-smoke

A portable application for FAT on the board's block storage: it waits up to
ten seconds for a device -- a USB flash drive on a PIO-USB host-port board --
mounts its FAT volume at "/usb" with mm.fs.fat, runs mm.fs.conformance's
checks inside it, prints the counts and the first failure on the console,
and unmounts. The checks work in a scratch directory and remove it; nothing
else on the drive is touched.

It never formats. A drive holding no FAT volume is reported and left alone.
It skips, exiting 0, on a board with no block storage or when no drive
appears.

Exit codes:

| Code | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| 0 | Every check passed, or there was no storage or no drive and the run skipped. |
| 1 | Mounting failed for another reason. |
| 2 | The drive holds no FAT volume; it was not formatted. |
| 3 | The checks could not run: the scratch directory could not be made. |
| 4 | Unmounting failed. |
| 5 | At least one check failed; the console names the first. |
